# Build output
bin/
obj/
*.user
artifacts/

# Local test data captured from the reference server
traces/
*.trace
*.gg2trace

# ...except the recordings the tests are built on. Those are oracles, not
# scratch data: WeaponBlockTests and PhysicsParityTests assert they exist, so
# without this a fresh clone fails two tests that pass on the machine that
# recorded them. docs/PARITY.md says parity fixtures live with the tests and
# run in CI; this is what makes that true.
!tests/Gg2.Tests/Fixtures/*.trace

# Claude Code session automation: the hooks, settings.json and commands that
# carry a handoff from one session to the next.
#
# ⚠️ The negation is load-bearing. ~/.gitignore_global excludes .claude/
# wholesale, and git will not descend into an excluded DIRECTORY to find a
# negated file inside it - so the directory has to be re-included first or
# .claude/hooks/ is silently untracked and a fresh clone gets none of it.
!.claude/

# ...but handoffs stay out. They are disposable messages to the next session,
# not documentation. See CLAUDE.md, "Where documentation goes".
.claude/notes/

# Machine-specific overrides, never team config.
.claude/settings.local.json

# The bot nav graphs. These are gg2-nav-gen's output, not the reference's and
# not this repo's source: 34 MB of hex for 24 map areas, rebuilt by running the
# generator. They used to be read out of the reference tree's GM8 build
# directory, which coupled the test suite to one particular checkout of a fork.
# ReferenceTree.NavCacheDirectory now looks here, or at GG2_NAVCACHE.
nav/
